Summary: wined3d: keep the mapped range for Wine's own buffers, so streamed draws don't flush whole buffers
Category: graphics
Kind: performance, fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: dlls/wined3d/buffer.c, buffer_resource_sub_resource_map()
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: WineHQ b6810e41 (11.22) marks the whole buffer dirty on every write map
 of a non-managed buffer, because applications write outside the range they
 lock. It also applies to the buffers wined3d and ddraw keep for themselves,
 such as the streaming buffer that DrawPrimitiveUP fills, though their
 writers stay inside the mapped range. Each small streamed draw then sends
 the whole buffer (512 KB or more) again. Iji (Game Maker 7, d3d8, ~557
 DrawPrimitiveUP quads a frame) ran its menu loop about 3x slower on 11.22
 than on 11.21. In tests/regress/d3d8-up-draw-speed the cost shows with
 software vertex processing only; with hardware vertex processing UP draws
 took the same time on 11.21 and 11.22. Buffers without a parent are the
 internal ones (every d3d8, d3d9, d3d11 and ddraw application buffer has
 one), so the whole-buffer rule now skips them; application buffers keep it.
Uncertain: whether every parentless buffer's writer stays inside its mapped
 range (wined3d's streaming buffers and push constants, ddraw's execute
 buffer copies were read and do).
Applies to: wine 11.22, macfixes
Status: 2026-11-17 in a quick build of macfixes 11.22 (VM, not for release).
 Iji on kiya (macOS 26, interleaved, 3 rounds): median main-loop gap
 74-79 ms, the same as 11.21-build8 (77-85 ms); 11.22-build7 219-259 ms.
 F12 quit Iji in 3 of 3 (2.7-2.9 s). d3d8-up-draw-speed on meeka (M1 Max,
 macOS 26.7): passes 3 of 3 (1.4-1.5x), fails 3 of 3 on 11.22-build7 and
 on plain 11.22-build1 (about 40x).
 2026-11-17 in wine-macfixes-11.22-build8 (draft): d3d8-up-draw-speed passes
 on meeka (1.6x). On a test Mac (macOS 26): Iji runs and quits from its
 menu; White Wolf passes from disc and in 4 of 5 Big Fish trial runs (the
 fifth failed in the test harness, not Wine); Bioscopia passes; nothing
 worse than build7. Second Chance's full set on build8 (kiya, macOS 26,
 muted): 36 of 36 disc games, 5 of 6 download games (Icy Tower fails in
 Second Chance's own msvcrt patch, not Wine). Iji's menu loop, 3
 interleaved rounds: 73-77 ms on build8, 73-74 ms on 11.21-build8, 222 ms
 on 11.22-build7.

--- a/dlls/wined3d/buffer.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/buffer.c
@@ -581,8 +581,15 @@
      * and Darkstar One write outside the range they map with DISCARD, and
      * Pure Pinball maps four bytes of a vertex buffer without flags and
      * writes all of it. Managed buffers are the exception; native only
-     * uploads the mapped range for those. */
-    if ((flags & WINED3D_MAP_WRITE) && !wined3d_resource_access_is_managed(resource->access))
+     * uploads the mapped range for those.
+     *
+     * Buffers without a parent belong to wined3d or the d3d front end
+     * itself (streaming buffers for DrawPrimitiveUP and friends, push
+     * constants, ddraw's internal buffers). Their writers stay inside the
+     * mapped range, and marking the whole buffer dirty there makes every
+     * small streaming write flush the whole buffer. */
+    if ((flags & WINED3D_MAP_WRITE) && !wined3d_resource_access_is_managed(resource->access)
+            && resource->parent)
     {
         dirty_offset = 0;
         dirty_size = 0;
